# Grafana Dashboard — Payment DB Health
Suggested panels (import from a Prometheus datasource connected to `postgres_exporter`/CNPG):
| Panel | Metric | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Replication Lag (s) | `pg_replication_lag_seconds` | Early detection of sync slowness/outage |
| Connected Standbys | `pg_stat_replication_count` | Verify Master-Slave connectivity |
| DELETE Rate | `rate(pg_stat_user_tables_n_tup_del{relname="payment_transactions"}[5m])` | Detect abnormal mass deletions |
| UPDATE Rate | `rate(pg_stat_user_tables_n_tup_upd{relname="payment_transactions"}[5m])` | Detect abnormal mass updates |
| INSERT Rate (Transaction Throughput) | `rate(pg_stat_user_tables_n_tup_ins{relname="payment_transactions"}[5m])` | Sudden drop = sign of downtime |
| WAL Generation Rate | `pg_stat_archiver_archived_count` | Abnormal WAL volume = suspicious activity |
| Active Connections by Role | `pg_stat_activity_count by (usename)` | Identify unauthorized direct connections to Master |
| Cluster Status (Primary/Standby) | `cnpg_collector_up` / CNPG native dashboard | Overall status from the operator's perspective |

The complete dashboard JSON file can be created and exported in Grafana based on this table later;
in this repository,rather than providing a pre-made JSON file (which depends on your specific
datasource setup),the panel structure is documented so it can be implemented directly.
